  "summary": "Four preprints pair physics-based sampling with learned latent spaces or generative models to map multiple binding modes and conformational states.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread treats biomolecular behavior as a conformational ensemble to be sampled, not a single structure. Two preprints apply enhanced sampling to multimodal binding: funnel-restrained TAMD on Martini 3 with beta-VAE latent-space clustering finds three recurring CYFIP1-eIF4E binding modes, and OneOPES simulations of FCP1 binding Rap74 reveal a multimodal landscape, with a new Divide et impera free-energy decomposition. REVEAL chains generative secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2 tertiary prediction, unbiased MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR RNA. What is new is the coupling of learned models with physics-based sampling. The simulated annealing paper on protein sequence design is peripheral, addressing inverse folding rather than ensembles.",
